Current gain factor, $\alpha=0.96R=1000 \Omega$, Voltage drop across collector resistor $=0.5 \mathrm{~V}\therefore \quad \beta=\frac{\alpha}{1-\alpha}=\frac{0.96}{1-0.96}=24\therefore$ Collector current,
$\begin{aligned}
i_c & =\frac{\text { Voltage drop across collector resistor }}{R} \\
& =\frac{0.5}{1000}=0.5 \times 10^{-3} \mathrm{~A}
\end{aligned}$
The base current, $i_b=\frac{i_c}{\beta}=\frac{0.5 \times 10^{-3}}{24}=20.8 \mu \mathrm{A}$

According to given truth table, logic expression of the output $Y$ for the given input $A$ and $B$ is given as

Y=\overline{A B}

which is the output expression for NAND gate.

In common base circuit, change in collector base voltage,

\begin{aligned}
&V_{C B}=0.6 \mathrm{~V} \\
&\Delta I_{C}=0.02 \mathrm{~mA}=2 \times 10^{-5} \mathrm{~A}
\end{aligned}

$\therefore$ Output resistance,

R_{\mathrm{out}}=\frac{\Delta V_{C B}}{\Delta I_{C}}=\frac{0.6}{2 \times 10^{-5}}=3 \times 10^{4} \Omega
